1 :=

   Assigns a string, the rest of the line, to a symbol.

   Format

     symbol-name :=[=] string

2 Parameters

 symbol-name

   The symbol.  ":=" makes it local to the command level, and ":=="
   global.  See Symbol_Assign.

 string

   The rest of the line.  Outside quotes, letters are made uppercase,
   runs of blanks become one, and a "!" begins a comment; quotes keep
   text as written, and are removed ("" inside them is a quote).
   Symbols between apostrophes are substituted first.

2 Examples

   1.$ LIST :== DIRECTORY/SIZE/DATE

     Makes LIST a command.

   2.$ TITLE := "Monthly Report"

     Gives TITLE the string Monthly Report, case and all.
